{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems"},"topicSections":[{"title":"Essentials","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/DeclaringSystems","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/DrivingAWorldFromAnApp","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System()","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System"],"anchor":"Essentials"},{"title":"System Parameters","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemParameter","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Update","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ResourceReader","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ResourceWriter","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/EventReader","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/EventWriter","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/RemovedComponents"],"anchor":"System-Parameters"},{"title":"Building and Running Schedules","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ScheduleBuilder","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ScheduledSystem","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemSet","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/CyclicOrdering","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Ambiguity"],"anchor":"Building-and-Running-Schedules"},{"title":"Main-Actor Systems","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/MainActorSystem"],"anchor":"Main-Actor-Systems"},{"title":"Built-In Systems","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/UpdateEvents","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ForwardEvents","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ForwardChanges"],"anchor":"Built-In-Systems"},{"title":"Profiling","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemProfile","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemTiming"],"anchor":"Profiling"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A world holds data: entities and their components, and resources. A "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"system"}]},{"type":"text","text":" holds a rule: a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"step that reads part of the world and changes part of it, such as “every entity with a velocity"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"moves” or “gravity pulls on everything that isn’t frozen.” A "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"schedule"}]},{"type":"text","text":" lists the systems of one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"frame or step and runs them on a world, each once per run."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The examples throughout this module use these components, resources and event:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["struct Position: Component { var x: Double, y: Double }","struct Velocity: Component { var dx: Double, dy: Double }","struct Health: Component { var current: Int }","struct Frozen: Component {}","","struct Score: Resource { var points: Int }","struct TimeStep: Resource { var seconds: Double }","struct Paused: Resource {}","","struct Damage: Event { var target: Entity, amount: Int }"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"text":"Declare a System","type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Declare-a-System"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The simplest way to write a system is to mark a type with the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@System"},{"text":" macro and give it a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"run","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" method. The method’s parameters say what the system works on, and their types say how:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"an ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Update","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" writes components, a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Query","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" reads them, and a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ResourceReader","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reads a resource. The following two systems pull everything that isn’t frozen downward, then move","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it by its velocity:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["@System","struct Gravity {","    func run(_ falling: Update<Velocity>.Where<Without<Frozen>>) {","        falling { velocity, _ in velocity.dy -= 10 }","    }","}","","@System","struct Movement {","    func run(_ movers: Update<Position>.Over<Velocity>.Where<Without<Frozen>>) {","        movers { position, row in","            position.x += row.components.dx","            position.y += row.components.dy","        }","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Because the parameters’ types state what each system reads and writes, the macro writes the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"system’s "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System\/access"},{"type":"text","text":" for you: "},{"code":"Gravity","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" writes "},{"code":"Velocity","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"; "},{"code":"Movement","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" writes "},{"code":"Position","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reads "},{"code":"Velocity","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". A schedule uses the access to decide which systems can run at the same time."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You can also conform a type to "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System"},{"type":"text","text":" by hand and write its "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System\/run(in:)"},{"type":"text","text":" method, which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"receives the whole world. See "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System"},{"type":"text","text":" for when to do that."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Run Systems in a Schedule","type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Run-Systems-in-a-Schedule"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" is built from a list of systems, written in a result builder. Running it runs each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"system once. The following example drops a ball for one frame:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["var world = World()","let ball = world.spawn(Position(x: 0, y: 100), Velocity(dx: 1, dy: 0))","","let frame = Schedule {","    Gravity()","    Movement().after(Gravity.self)","}","frame.run(on: &world)","","print(world[Position.self, of: ball])","\/\/ Prints \"Position(x: 1.0, y: 90.0)\""],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Systems run in the order you write them, unless an ordering constraint says otherwise."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"after(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"before(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" require one system to run after or before another; "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemSet","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"names a group of systems so constraints can refer to all of them at once; and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"runIf(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" skips"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a system when a condition doesn’t hold."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Systems whose accesses don’t conflict, because neither writes what the other reads or writes,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"run at the same time, and the world ends as though they had run one after another (commands","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"apply when each wave finishes). Systems that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"conflict run in order. When two conflicting systems aren’t ordered by any constraint, their order","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"rests only on how they happen to be written; ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/ambiguities()","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" finds those pairs so a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"test can keep a schedule free of them.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"symbolKind":"module","modules":[{"name":"Systems"}],"title":"Systems","roleHeading":"Framework","externalID":"Systems","role":"collection"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"text":"Declare the rules of a simulation as systems, and run them on a world in a schedule.","type":"text"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/systems"]}],"kind":"symbol","references":{"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/ScheduledSystem":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A system together with the ordering constraints, sets and conditions a schedule runs it with."}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ScheduledSystem","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"ScheduledSystem","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/scheduledsystem","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ScheduledSystem","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ScheduledSystem"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/SystemParameter":{"abstract":[{"text":"A type a system’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"run","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" method can take in place of the whole world, whose type states what","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the system reads and writes.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/systemparameter","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SystemParameter","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SystemParameter","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemParameter","type":"topic","title":"SystemParameter"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/ForwardChanges":{"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/forwardchanges","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ForwardChanges","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ForwardChanges","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A system that yields each component of one type added or changed since it last ran to an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"asynchronous stream, with its entity.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ForwardChanges","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"ForwardChanges"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/SystemSet":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemSet","abstract":[{"text":"A type that names a group of systems, so ordering constraints can refer to all of them at","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"once.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","title":"SystemSet","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/systemset","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SystemSet","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SystemSet","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/ForwardEvents":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ForwardEvents","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ForwardEvents","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A system that yields each event of one type to an asynchronous stream, so code outside the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"schedule can await the events.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ForwardEvents","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"ForwardEvents","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/forwardevents"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/EventWriter":{"title":"EventWriter","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/EventWriter","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"EventWriter"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A system parameter that sends events of one type."}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"EventWriter"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/eventwriter"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/RemovedComponents":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A system parameter that lists the entities that lost a component since the system last read"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"them."}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"RemovedComponents","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/RemovedComponents","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"RemovedComponents","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"RemovedComponents","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/removedcomponents","role":"symbol"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/DrivingAWorldFromAnApp":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/DrivingAWorldFromAnApp","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Hold a world in your app or game engine, feed it each frame’s input, and let the objects outside"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it read results and take part in a step."}],"role":"article","title":"Driving a World from an App","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/drivingaworldfromanapp"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Declare the rules of a simulation as systems, and run them on a world in a schedule.","type":"text"}],"role":"collection","title":"Systems","url":"\/documentation\/systems","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Schedule":{"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/schedule","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Schedule","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A list of systems that run on a world, in order, and at the same time where they can."}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Schedule","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"Schedule"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/System":{"abstract":[{"text":"A rule that reads and changes a world, run once each time its schedule runs.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"System","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"System","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"System","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/system","role":"symbol"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/System()":{"abstract":[{"text":"Makes a type a system whose access comes from the parameters of its ","type":"text"},{"code":"run","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" method.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"macro","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"System","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"()","kind":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System()","title":"System()","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/system()","role":"symbol"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/ResourceWriter":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ResourceWriter","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ResourceWriter","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A system parameter that reads and writes a resource.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ResourceWriter","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"ResourceWriter","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/resourcewriter"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/CyclicOrdering":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/CyclicOrdering","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"An error indicating that the ordering constraints of a schedule’s systems form a cycle, so no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"order satisfies them all.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","title":"CyclicOrdering","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/cyclicordering","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"CyclicOrdering","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"CyclicOrdering","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/MainActorSystem":{"abstract":[{"text":"A system that runs on the main actor, for work that touches main-actor state such as a user","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"interface.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/mainactorsystem","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MainActorSystem","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MainActorSystem","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/MainActorSystem","type":"topic","title":"MainActorSystem"},"doc://WorldModule/documentation/WorldModule/Query":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Query","title":"Query","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Query","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A description of the entities to visit and the components to read from each.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Query","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/worldmodule\/query","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/DeclaringSystems":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/DeclaringSystems","abstract":[{"text":"Write the rules of a simulation as systems, and let their parameters state what they read and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"write.","type":"text"}],"role":"collectionGroup","title":"Declaring Systems","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/declaringsystems"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Update":{"abstract":[{"text":"A system parameter that changes a component of every entity that holds it.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Update","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Update","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Update","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"Update","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/update","role":"symbol"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/System/run(in:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/system\/run(in:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System\/run(in:)","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"run"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"in"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"inout"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11WorldModule0A0V","text":"World"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Runs the system’s rule once on a world.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","required":true,"kind":"symbol","title":"run(in:)"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/EventReader":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/EventReader","abstract":[{"text":"A system parameter that reads the events of one type sent since the system last read them.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","title":"EventReader","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/eventreader","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"EventReader","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EventReader","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/ScheduleBuilder":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ScheduleBuilder","title":"ScheduleBuilder","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ScheduleBuilder","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A result builder that collects the systems written in a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule","type":"reference"},{"text":"’s closure.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ScheduleBuilder","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/schedulebuilder","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/SystemProfile":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemProfile","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/systemprofile","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SystemProfile","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A resource that records how long each system takes to run.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SystemProfile","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"SystemProfile"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Ambiguity":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Ambiguity","abstract":[{"text":"Two systems of a schedule whose accesses conflict but that no ordering constraint orders, so","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the order they run in rests only on the order they were written in.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","title":"Ambiguity","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/ambiguity","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Ambiguity"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Ambiguity"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/ResourceReader":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ResourceReader","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ResourceReader","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A system parameter that reads a resource.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ResourceReader","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"ResourceReader","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/resourcereader"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/SystemTiming":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemTiming","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SystemTiming","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The times one system of a schedule has taken to run.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SystemTiming","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"SystemTiming","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/systemtiming"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/System/access":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System\/access","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/system\/access","defaultImplementations":1,"type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"access"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Access","preciseIdentifier":"s:11WorldModule6AccessV"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The component, resource and event types the system reads and writes, or ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" if it may","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"change anything.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","required":true,"title":"access","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/UpdateEvents":{"abstract":[{"text":"A system that ends the current event update, dropping events old enough that every reader","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"has had its chance to read them.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"UpdateEvents","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/UpdateEvents","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"UpdateEvents","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"UpdateEvents","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/updateevents","role":"symbol"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Schedule/ambiguities()":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Returns every pair of systems whose accesses conflict but that no ordering constraint"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"orders."}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ambiguities"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> ["},{"text":"Ambiguity","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Systems9AmbiguityV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/ambiguities()","title":"ambiguities()","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/schedule\/ambiguities()","role":"symbol"}}}